# A. You Can Use This – But With Limits

You (the person reading this) are absolutely welcome to **use this code**, run it on your machine, use it, share it. That’s cool. That’s what it’s here for.

But here's the thing: this code is being given to you under a very specific set of rules. You can use it **as-is**, for **non-commercial** purposes, **without modification**, and only **if you credit me – XKITZ – as the original creator**. You’re not buying this. You’re not licensing it for your startup. You’re not uploading it to your GitHub as your own. You’re borrowing it under strict terms.

